## 1. Executive adjudication

[INFERENCE] **Retain LC-SRS for exactly one prospectively registered successor TRAIN gate; do not promote CSE or EC, and do not authorize execution now.** The reported R6 raw predicate fails. That prevents R6 acceptance, but does not invalidate the LC-SRS identity or establish that an independent test is scientifically illegitimate. My continuation decision requires **raw and balanced criteria jointly**, not permission to accept whichever becomes favorable (`CLAIM-CEILING.md`, lines 5–20).

[ABSENT-AT-CHECK] Neither optional direct artifact—`evidence/R6-FIT-SCREEN-VERIFIED.json` or `reviews/ASTRA-ULTRA-PROCESS-ADJUDICATION.md`—is present. R6 values, runtime stoppage, correction status, and Astra’s direction therefore retain their handoff provenance. Missing copies do not establish that the underlying work never occurred (`CURRENT-STATUS.md`, lines 126–138).

[INFERENCE] Scientific continuation and integration readiness differ. The frozen method is reviewable; the successor contract is not launch-ready; the five-arm system remains an execution seam. The supplied evidence supports neither immediate structural rejection of C3 nor automatic contingency promotion.

## 2. R6 arithmetic, metric legitimacy, and claim boundary

[HANDOFF-VERIFIED] Informed and matched-placebo raw accuracies are respectively 0.8293051359516616 and 0.7915407854984894; informed Spearman is 0.8367467202782021 (`CURRENT-STATUS.md`, lines 43–61).

[INFERENCE] Their difference is

$$
0.03776435045317217<0.05,
$$

missing the frozen requirement by **1.223565 percentage points**. High Spearman cannot compensate: these are conjunctive predicates, not components of a weighted acceptance score.

[COPIED-AUTHORITY] The calculator selects targets with \(|\bar y|\ge0.02\), compares prediction and target signs, pools held-out rows once per seed, and averages three seed metrics. It requires Spearman ≥0.20, raw accuracy ≥0.60, and raw advantage ≥0.05, alongside world-stability requirements (`fast-screen/compute_fit_screen.py`, lines 49–53, 95–164).

[INFERENCE] With 1,038 positive and 286 negative rows, an always-positive predictor obtains \(1038/1324=0.7839879\). Raw accuracy equals

$$
A=\pi\,TPR+(1-\pi)\,TNR,
$$

where \(\pi=0.7839879\); balanced accuracy gives each conditional recall half the weight. Raw accuracy can therefore appear strong despite weak negative-sign recognition. However, both arms encounter the same prevalence: imbalance neither invalidates their raw difference nor proves why it failed (`CURRENT-STATUS.md`, lines 51–76).

[INFERENCE] Averaging the rounded development balanced values gives informed/placebo means 0.678333/0.578700, with difference 0.099633. These motivate a new question, not an R6 pass. Their confusion matrices and complete aggregation specification are unavailable. Ranking, sign discrimination, and action-useful calibration remain different properties.

[PROPOSAL] Equal-sign weighting is a legitimate prospective complement because recognizing harmful credits matters alongside recognizing beneficial ones. Freeze its population, denominators, aggregation, and decision role before fresh outcomes. No retrospective substitution, old/new outcome pooling, or second metric revision is admissible.

[INFERENCE] Crucially, the **reported raw failure is not an authenticated whole-run scientific token**. The stopped runtime still faces integrity-first verification. Neither runtime repair nor balanced reanalysis can make the reported raw predicate pass (`authority/LC-SRS-GATE-CONTRACT.md`, §§13–14).

## 3. Scientific legitimacy of LC-SRS and integration-readiness audit

[COPIED-AUTHORITY] With \(G(x)=B(x)-\lambda E(x)\), the teacher defines \(d_i=\ell_i+e_i=G(x_i)-G(00)\), interaction \(\Psi=G(11)-G(10)-G(01)+G(00)\), and \(z_{3,i}=e_i+\Psi/2\). Consequently,

$$
\sum_i(\ell_i+z_{3,i})=d_1+d_2+\Psi=G(11)-G(00).
$$

Surplus terms have units of bits; division by \(\kappa\) occurs once. Exactness covers the specified two-user current-slot game—not arbitrary coalitions, partial adoption, learned Q1, or simultaneous full-roster decisions (`authority/LC-SRS-GATE-CONTRACT.md`, §§3.2, 5).

[INFERENCE] Exact surplus attribution is not exact EE improvement: ratio direction depends on \(\Delta B-\eta(00)\Delta E\), not necessarily frozen-\(\lambda\) surplus. Nor does learning \(z_3\) establish that Q1 supplies the required \(\ell_i\). Separate calibration and physical comparisons are indispensable (`authority/LC-SRS-GATE-CONTRACT.md`, §§5, 9–12).

[COPIED-AUTHORITY] C3View is deterministic conditional on captured predecision inputs. Detached Q1/Q2 can inherit ordinary observation-time SINR ancestry; detachment removes gradients, not ancestry. Direct SINR tokens, fresh encoder draws, privileged teacher outcomes, and postdecision information are forbidden. Deployment retains one scalar Q3, one common native safe mask, and one literal masked \(Q1+Q2+Q3\) argmax without coordination or repair (`authority/LC-SRS-GATE-CONTRACT.md`, §3).

[COPIED-AUTHORITY] The freeze records implementation-bound audits and 62 focused test passes, while explicitly recording execution `NO-GO`. These are copied audit reports, not reproduced physical-run evidence (`authority/METHOD-FREEZE.md`, lines 3–6, 29–58).

[INFERENCE] “Observable” requires leakage-free held-out information beyond matched placebo; “learnable” requires the fixed student to meet cross-world predicates; “composable” requires successful literal full-roster selection and service guards. “Efficacious” requires separately admitted physical policy comparisons with genuine retrained source ablations. Oracle signs, checksums, and fit associations establish none of that final efficacy claim (`authority/LC-SRS-GATE-CONTRACT.md`, §§7–14).

[COPIED-AUTHORITY] The five-arm runner delegates physical execution to injected callbacks; its CLI performs preflight only. Its tests generate synthetic bits/energy, and result aggregation leaves `scientific_decision=None` (`five-arm/v023_real_five_arm_episode_runner.py`, lines 615–649, 1006–1027; `five-arm/test_v023_real_five_arm_episode_runner.py`, lines 186–216; `five-arm/v023_five_arm_eval_results.py`, lines 295–348).

[INFERENCE] Thus the runner, binding, results module, and tests establish reviewable plumbing—not a real five-arm run. The five policy arms—FULL, explicit pre-Catfish BASELINE, and three retrained source ablations—must also not be confused with the gate’s informed/placebo/zero/oracle panel. Zero Q3 is not that policy BASELINE (`five-arm/FIVE-ARM-EVALUATION-README.md`; `five-arm/v023_five_arm_eval_binding.py`).

## 4. Process-flaw and evidence-provenance audit

[COPIED-AUTHORITY] The earlier receipt defect confused `LCSRSAnchorSurface.content_digest` with `LCSRSAnchorRecord.content_digest`; the latter additionally binds world, phase, anchor, and detached-Q12 provenance. The prescribed R6 correction rebinds ordered full-record identities while preserving targets, losses, updates, parameters, and thresholds, with wrong-domain rejection retained (`authority/R6-RELAUNCH-DECISION.md`, lines 30–71).

[INFERENCE] This is an execution-binding correction, not permission to weaken verification. Digest fields require explicit domains and schemas; a matching hash does not independently authenticate the causal provenance claimed for its contents.

[HANDOFF-VERIFIED] The separate composition replay/runtime defect stopped full R6, with evidence retained. C1/C2 target generation first failed before physics because `_network_snapshot` was referenced at the wrong module level; correction/relaunch remained in progress (`CURRENT-STATUS.md`, lines 78–98).

[INFERENCE] Neither is a scientific negative result. Neither a corrected import nor successful replay reverses raw failure. Production-path regression and authenticated completed receipts remain necessary: “tested,” “launched,” and “running” are not completed target generation. The older “R6 PREPARED; NOT LAUNCHED” document describes an earlier state, not a contradiction of the later handoff.

[INFERENCE] The fast screen does not authenticate manifests or independently prove unique SUPPORTED-row membership. Its world-rank comparison uses ordinary strict comparison rather than the contract’s tolerance. It cannot replace the final verifier, and these limitations do not rescue the raw shortfall (`fast-screen/compute_fit_screen.py`, lines 56–93, 109–126; `authority/LC-SRS-GATE-CONTRACT.md`, §§12–14).

[COPIED-AUTHORITY] The older episode specification leaves HEAD_DROP versus SOURCE_ABLATION unresolved, whereas the controlling gate and binding require retrained source ablations. The runner also explicitly binds the old gate-contract hash (`five-arm/EPISODE-SCREEN-SPEC.md`, lines 107–119; `five-arm/v023_five_arm_eval_binding.py`, lines 340–408; `five-arm/v023_real_five_arm_episode_runner.py`, lines 417–420).

[INFERENCE] Successor admission therefore requires new bindings, not reuse of R6 authorization. Preregistering this adaptively motivated development test also does not erase earlier attempts or establish familywise error control. Development-versus-efficacy language and retention of failed evidence are essential safeguards against metric shopping.

## 5. LC-SRS versus CSE versus EC disposition

[COPIED-AUTHORITY] The locked order is LC-SRS, CSE, then EC; observability failure does not automatically promote the contingencies. Their energy-unit formulas are

$$
z_D=\Delta B_{-u}-\lambda(\Delta share_u-\Delta E),\qquad
z_F=-\lambda(\Delta share_u-\Delta E),
$$

using unilateral branches and joule-valued shares. Both targets are bit-valued (`authority/CONTINGENCY-LADDER.md`, §§2, 4).

[INFERENCE] **CSE’s “joint exact” argument fails.** Conservation \(\sum_u share_u(x)=E(x)\) within one configuration does not identify sums evaluated across distinct unilateral configurations \(c^u\). The root counterexample produces summed unilateral combined credits \(+0.5\), while simultaneous true surplus is \(-0.25\). That directly defeats the asserted implication, without proving CSE useless as a heuristic (`authority/FABLE-C3-SOURCE-AUDIT.md`, §7D; `authority/ROOT-FABLE-C3-ADJUDICATION.md`, lines 53–115).

[ABSENT-AT-CHECK] The supplied package contains no admitted CSE/EC promotion result. This is an evidence gap, not a failed experiment.

[INFERENCE] Removing the external-rate term does not itself establish EC’s superiority. Neither contingency earns promotion through simplicity or physical plausibility. LC-SRS retains its narrower valid identity, while the reported failure concerns learner acceptance.

[COPIED-AUTHORITY] Fable’s later LC-SRS audit warns that favorable joint adoption can depend on Q1/Q2 calibration and coexist with harmful partial adoption; it does not guarantee decentralized composition (`authority/FABLE-51-C3-POSTGATE-AUDIT.md`, lines 40–75).

## 6. One exact next contract

[PROPOSAL] **Scope and admission.** Freeze one successor, `LC-SRS-FRESH-SIGN-1`, for current-slot TRAIN observability/composition only. No episode-policy training, five-arm episode evaluation, or TEST. This read-only review is **non-heavy**. The physical scan plus 48 fixed fits is **heavy**, belongs on Ubuntu, and requires new authorization; projected simulator/multi-world work exceeding approximately 30 minutes is heavy. A verified four-profile/composition path is prerequisite; a completed five-arm episode adapter is not required for this narrower gate.

[PROPOSAL] **Population and pairing.** Reserve ordered TRAIN worlds `2026121731`–`2026121738`, conditional on an authenticated ledger proving them unopened. These are proposed identifiers, not verified-unused assets; absent proof blocks admission, without automatic substitution. Exclude previous R6/V0.22 and reserved contingency worlds. Preserve lineage `2026092101`, rung `003000`, the exact checkpoint digest in gate §2.1, and seeds `2026135101`–`2026135103`. Pair arms within world/fold/seed. Retain anchors 1–9, outcome-blind pair enumeration, eight leave-one-world-out folds, and 32 common-field draws. Field keys exclude arm, pair, and profile.

[PROPOSAL] **Method and comparators.** Preserve LC-SRS, \(\lambda=118424222.8550065\) bit/J, \(\kappa=10097071012.757404\) bits, their frozen hexadecimal representations, C3View, 67–64–64–1 scorer, optimizer, S/R/C loss, and 2,000 updates. Fit INFORMED and MATCHED-PLACEBO only: 48 models. Retain ZERO-SURFACE \(B=Q1+Q2\) and TEACHER-ORACLE diagnostics. Preserve gate §7’s training-world strata, cyclic permutations, unchanged held-out labels, and ≥80% placebo eligibility per fold. No sign-reweighted training or candidate variants.

[PROPOSAL] **Balanced estimand.** For arm \(h\), world \(w\), seed \(k\), let \(P_w,N_w\) contain unique SUPPORTED rows with \(\bar y\ge0.02\) and \(\bar y\le-0.02\):

$$
BA_{hwk}=\frac12\left[
\frac{\sum_{r\in P_w}\mathbf1(\widehat y_{hwkr}>0)}{|P_w|}
+\frac{\sum_{r\in N_w}\mathbf1(\widehat y_{hwkr}<0)}{|N_w|}
\right],
\qquad BA_h=\frac1{24}\sum_{w,k}BA_{hwk}.
$$

Predictions remain \(Q3(s_r,a_r)-Q3(s_r,a_r^{ref})\). Require both classes in every world and ≥24 unique rows per class overall; insufficient support stops observability without replacement sampling. Zero predictions are errors. Small/zero targets, unsupported, reference, control, and masked rows remain separately accounted for, outside sign denominators. Nonfinite labels/predictions invalidate execution; undefined correlations fail their existing predicate.

[PROPOSAL] **One acceptance rule.** Require informed Spearman ≥0.20, original raw accuracy ≥0.60, original raw advantage ≥0.05, **and** \(BA_I\ge0.60\), \(BA_I-BA_P\ge0.05\). Preserve informed mean-seed Spearman superiority in ≥6/8 worlds and each informed seed’s nonnegative Spearman in ≥5/8 worlds. These are operational thresholds, not significance levels. Report original row-pooled/seed-averaged raw metrics, equal-world balanced metrics, confusion counts, exclusions, and paired world/seed results. Worlds—not rows, draws, or initialization seeds—are physical clusters. No post-outcome metric or aggregation choice.

[PROPOSAL] **Physical/composition/service conjunction.** Retain gate §§10–12: ≥24 pairs and ≥1/world; ≥90% passing complete per-draw mechanics, with no unresolved formula, common-field, mask, or mutation errors; positive pooled 11-versus-00 EE and ≥4/8 positive worlds. Require action change ≥10%, literal 11 ≥25% and present in ≥4/8 worlds, harmful partials ≤5%, and topology consistency ≥80% among selected-11 pairs; zero selected-11 denominator fails. Oracle and informed full-roster EE must each exceed B pooled and in ≥4/8 worlds. Every world must satisfy \(S_I\ge S_B-0.01\). Preserve nonmember destination persistence, source-closure/no-new-destination checks, negative controls, identity tolerance, and bits/energy/lower-tail-service receipts. Pool physical totals separately per seed before averaging seed-level ratios; retain the frozen direction tolerances.

[PROPOSAL] **Preregistration and provenance.** Obtain timestamped controller acceptance before any fresh outcome. Bind contract, access ledger, physical source/runtime/TLE closure, Q12 observation-event ancestry, full anchor-record and surface digest domains, targets/profiles, field keys, masks, permutations, folds, initialization/configuration, and verifier. Authenticate production-path correction and composition-replay regressions first. Retain independent C1/C2 context predicates from gate §9: missing authentication is invalidity; a valid weak diagnostic is HOLD, not C3 rescue.

[PROPOSAL] **Hard stop.** Independently recompute all predicates from immutable receipts, preserving §14’s integrity-first precedence. Any scientific failure terminates this successor route: no second metric revision, added seed, replacement world, formula adjustment, or automatic contingency promotion. Invalid execution receives neither a scientific pass nor automatic retry authorization. Success permits only the next separately reviewed contract—not episode training or efficacy claims.

## 7. Risks, falsifiers, and remaining claim ceiling

[INFERENCE] Principal risks are minority-class scarcity, placebo-preserved generic propensity, dependence on one Q12 lineage, teacher information outside deployable inputs, calibration mismatch, and simultaneous actions invalidating reference topology. Balanced accuracy addresses class weighting alone (`authority/LC-SRS-GATE-CONTRACT.md`, §§3, 7, 9–12).

[PROPOSAL] Distinguish failed physics as a mechanism falsifier, failed held-out discrimination as an observability/learner falsifier, and successful discrimination with failed adoption/service as an interface-composition falsifier. None automatically means “C3 is impossible.”

[COPIED-AUTHORITY] Even a complete successor pass remains TRAIN-development evidence, not three positive Catfish marginals, FULL-over-ablation ordering, deployment readiness, or EE efficacy (`CLAIM-CEILING.md`, lines 22–38).

## 8. Final decision

[INFERENCE] Continue the **candidate**, not failed R6 acceptance or unready execution. One independent successor with conjunctive raw/balanced requirements and unchanged physical/composition/service safeguards is defensible. CSE’s exactness argument fails; neither contingency has earned promotion. Integration gaps block launch, not this bounded scientific disposition.

